## 🚀 PART 1 — Deploy to Vercel (Step by Step)

### Step 1 — Get Your Gemini API Key (Free)

1. Go to **https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey**
2. Sign in with your Google account
3. Click **"Create API Key"**
4. Copy the key — it looks like: `AIzaSy...`

---

### Step 2 — Install Node.js & Vercel CLI

```powershell
# Check if Node.js is installed
node --version

# If not installed, download from https://nodejs.org (LTS version)

# Install Vercel CLI globally
npm install -g vercel
```

---

### Step 3 — Create a GitHub Repository

1. Go to **https://github.com/new**
2. Repository name: `naturize`
3. Set to **Public** (required for free Vercel hosting)
4. Click **"Create repository"**

Then push your project:

```powershell
cd C:\Users\acer\Desktop\Projects\humanize

git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit — Naturize AI SaaS"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/YOUR_USERNAME/naturize.git
git push -u origin main
```

---

### Step 4 — Deploy to Vercel

**Option A — Via Vercel Dashboard (Recommended)**

1. Go to **https://vercel.com** → Sign up with GitHub
2. Click **"Add New Project"**
3. Import your `naturize` GitHub repository
4. Leave all settings as default
5. Click **"Deploy"**
6. Wait ~60 seconds — you get a live URL like `naturize.vercel.app`

**Option B — Via CLI**

```powershell
cd C:\Users\acer\Desktop\Projects\humanize
vercel
# Follow prompts → link to your Vercel account
# Select "yes" to all defaults
```

---

### Step 5 — Add Your Gemini API Key (CRITICAL)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Without this step the app will show errors. Do this AFTER deploying.

1. Go to **https://vercel.com/dashboard**
2. Click your **naturize** project
3. Go to **Settings → Environment Variables**
4. Click **"Add New"**
5. Fill in:
   - **Key:** `GEMINI_API_KEY`
   - **Value:** paste your Gemini key (`AIzaSy...`)
   - **Environment:** ✅ Production ✅ Preview ✅ Development
6. Click **"Save"**
7. Go to **Deployments → Redeploy** (top right → "Redeploy")

✅ Your app is now live and working!

---

### Step 6 — Use a Custom Domain (Optional but recommended)

1. Buy a domain on **Hostinger / GoDaddy / Namecheap** (~₹600/year)
2. In Vercel → Project → Settings → **Domains**
3. Add your domain e.g. `naturize.app`
4. Follow the DNS instructions Vercel shows you
5. SSL certificate is **automatic and free**

---

### Step 7 — Test Locally Before Deploying Changes

```powershell
cd C:\Users\acer\Desktop\Projects\humanize

# Create local env file
copy .env.example .env.local
# Open .env.local and add your real key

# Install vercel CLI locally
npm install

# Run dev server
npm run dev
# Opens at http://localhost:3000
```

---

## 💰 PART 2 — Make Money from Ads (Google AdSense)

### How AdSense Works

- Google places ads on your site automatically
- You earn money every time someone **views** or **clicks** an ad
- Typical earnings: **₹10–₹80 per 1,000 visitors** (varies by niche)
- AI tools get **higher-than-average CPM** (₹40–₹150/1000 visitors)
- Payment is monthly via bank transfer (minimum ₹8,000 threshold)

---

### Step 1 — Apply for Google AdSense

> [!IMPORTANT]
> AdSense requires your site to have **real traffic and content** before approval. Apply after getting your first 200+ visitors.

1. Go to **https://adsense.google.com**
2. Sign in with a Gmail account
3. Click **"Get Started"**
4. Enter your website URL (e.g. `https://naturize.app`)
5. Choose your country → India
6. Accept terms → Click **"Start using AdSense"**

**What Google checks:**
- ✅ Site is live and accessible
- ✅ Has original, useful content (Naturize qualifies)
- ✅ Privacy Policy page exists
- ✅ Terms of Service page exists
- ✅ No prohibited content

**Approval time:** 2–14 days

---

### Step 2 — Add Privacy Policy & Terms Pages

Google **requires** these. Create simple pages:

```
https://naturize.app/privacy
https://naturize.app/terms
```

You can use free generators:
- **https://www.privacypolicygenerator.info**
- **https://www.termsfeed.com/free-tools/terms-of-service-generator**

Create `privacy.html` and `terms.html` in your project with the generated text.

---

### Step 3 — Activate AdSense After Approval

Once approved, Google gives you an AdSense publisher ID like:
`ca-pub-1234567890123456`

**Replace the ad placeholders in `index.html`:**

```html
<!-- BEFORE (placeholder): -->
<div class="ad-banner ad-banner--728">Advertisement</div>

<!-- AFTER (real AdSense): -->
<ins class="adsbygoogle"
     style="display:block;width:728px;height:90px;"
     data-ad-client="ca-pub-YOUR_ID_HERE"
     data-ad-slot="YOUR_SLOT_ID"
     data-ad-format="auto"></ins>
<script>(adsbygoogle = window.adsbygoogle || []).push({});</script>
```

Also add the AdSense script tag in `<head>` of `index.html`:
```html
<script async src="https://pagead2.googlesyndication.com/pagead/js/adsbygoogle.js?client=ca-pub-YOUR_ID_HERE"
     crossorigin="anonymous"></script>
```

---

### Step 4 — Revenue Expectations

| Monthly Visitors | Estimated Monthly Revenue |
|-----------------|--------------------------|
| 1,000 | ₹100 – ₹500 |
| 5,000 | ₹500 – ₹2,500 |
| 20,000 | ₹2,000 – ₹10,000 |
| 100,000 | ₹10,000 – ₹50,000 |
| 500,000 | ₹50,000 – ₹2,50,000+ |

> AI tools like humanizers get **3–5x higher RPM** than average sites because users are motivated (students, writers, professionals).

---

### Step 5 — Drive Traffic (SEO Strategy)

The app is already SEO-optimized. To get traffic:

**Free methods:**
1. **Reddit** — Post in r/ChatGPT, r/AItools, r/StudyTips with your tool link
2. **Quora** — Answer "How to bypass AI detection?" with your link
3. **YouTube Shorts** — Show the tool in action (30-second demo)
4. **Twitter/X** — Tweet at AI influencers with your tool
5. **Product Hunt** — Launch at https://producthunt.com (free, huge exposure)

**SEO keywords already in your site:**
- `AI Humanizer` — 40,000+ monthly searches
- `Humanize AI Text` — 30,000+ monthly searches
- `AI Text Detector` — 25,000+ monthly searches

---

### Step 6 — Premium Subscriptions (Future)

When you have 1,000+ users/month, add Razorpay for ₹199/month payments:

1. Create account at **https://razorpay.com**
2. Add Razorpay checkout to the "Upgrade" buttons
3. Create a backend `/api/verify-payment` endpoint
4. Store premium user status in a database (Vercel KV or Supabase — both have free tiers)

